# ---- lane heartbeat reaper (optional — hub only) ----
# bin/heartbeat-reaper.sh (cron/hub.cron, */5) reads state/heartbeat/<lane>.<pid>.json
# and pages ONCE through bin/lane-alert.sh for a lane instance that went silent
# (now - last_tick past interval x HB_STALE_MULT, never under HB_SILENT_FLOOR_S
# seconds; 0 = no floor) or died. HB_MASS_STALE_N findings
# in one pass collapse to a single line (a hub reboot kills every lane at once); a
# dead lane is relaunched at most HB_RESTART_PER_HOUR times an hour and only if it
# declared a restart command; a file marked stale for HB_STALE_GC_S is collected.
# None is required — the code defaults are the five values below. The reaper reads
# these lines out of THIS FILE itself (the cron line passes it no environment):
# HB_<NAME>=<digits> only, a non-numeric value is ignored and the default stands,
# and a value already in the environment wins. docs/verification-map/lane-heartbeat.md
# A lane that declares `cron` (merge-conductor) is judged by its last completed tick in
# state/heartbeat-done/<lane> (interval from its catalog cadence x HB_STALE_MULT); a killed cron tick is not a page.
#HB_STALE_MULT=3
#HB_SILENT_FLOOR_S=120
#HB_MASS_STALE_N=3
#HB_RESTART_PER_HOUR=3
#HB_STALE_GC_S=86400

